  "as_of": "2019-02-13",
  "sentences": [
   "The bill would increase and extend the instant asset write-off available to small businesses, allowing larger eligible asset costs to be deducted immediately.",
   "It would lift the threshold from $20,000 to $25,000 for qualifying assets first used or ready for use from 29 January 2019 until 30 June 2020.",
   "The proposal would cover small businesses with aggregated annual turnover below $10 million, with the usual $1,000 threshold returning from 1 July 2020."
  ],
  "changes": [
   "Qualifying small business pool balances below $25,000 could also be deducted in full.",
   "The higher threshold would extend to eligible later costs of assets already written off.",
   "Relief from the five-year restriction on re-entering simplified depreciation would continue for another year."
  ],
  "affected": "Small business entities using, or seeking to return to, the simplified depreciation rules are affected.",
